ue with an element of the sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The final accumulated value. If the sequence has no elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the result is ","type":"text"},{"code":"initialResult","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce(into:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method to produce a single value from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements of an entire sequence. For example, you can use this method on an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array of integers to filter adjacent equal entries or count frequencies.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This method is preferred over ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for efficiency when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"result is a copy-on-write type, for example an Array or a Dictionary.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"updateAccumulatingResult","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure is called sequentially with a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mutable accumulating value initialized to ","type":"text"},{"code":"initialResult","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and each element","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"of the sequence. This example shows how to build a dictionary of letter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"frequencies of a string.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let letters = \"abracadabra\"","let letterCount = letters.reduce(into: [:]) { counts, letter in"," 